---
title: M-Ranked — Telegram collection sequence
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant S as Scheduler
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant T as Telegram adapter
    participant API as MTProto
    participant WEB as t.me public web
    participant TW as Telegram Web comments
    participant P as Canonical pipeline
    participant R as Redis

    S->>R: Acquire telegram partition lease
    S->>DB: Start collection_run and load enabled accounts
    loop For each account within concurrency limit
        S->>T: collect(account, access_mode, cursor)
        alt access_mode = mtproto
            T->>API: get_entity(username)
            API-->>T: channel identity and metadata
            T->>API: iter_messages(limit, min_id with overlap)
            API-->>T: recent messages
            T->>T: Group albums and resolve logical publication identity
            T->>DB: Load bounded circular tracked page + member IDs + cursor
            opt Due IDs are outside recent window
                T->>API: get_messages(ids)
                API-->>T: refreshed messages or missing IDs
            end
            opt FloodWait
                API-->>T: FloodWait(seconds)
                T->>T: Wait once, retry account, then record failure
            end
        else access_mode = public_web
            T->>WEB: GET /s/{username}
            WEB-->>T: Preview page, posts and rounded subscribers
            opt Subscriber metadata is due
                T->>WEB: GET /{username}
                WEB-->>T: Exact count when exposed, otherwise rounded value
            end
            T->>DB: Load bounded circular tracked page + refresh cursor
            opt Due publication is outside preview
                T->>WEB: GET /{username}/{messageId}?embed=1
                WEB-->>T: Post or 404/410/not-found marker
            end
            opt Telegram Web comments session enabled
                T->>TW: Batch-read comments for due message IDs
                TW-->>T: Counts or isolated comments error
            end
        end

        T->>P: Raw account, publications, counters and source metadata
        P->>P: Normalize IDs, reaction breakdown, views and comments
        P->>P: Apply sampling/completeness and NULL-vs-zero rules
        P->>P: Confirm only repeated authoritative point-lookup misses
        P->>DB: Transactional publications, snapshots, probes and refresh cursor
        DB-->>P: Commit with dataset revision
        P->>R: Publish revision.changed after commit
        P->>DB: Complete account result
    end
    S->>DB: Complete collection_run
    S->>R: Release/expire lease

    Note over T,P: Public preview is lower-quality evidence than MTProto,<br/>quality and access_mode remain attached to observations.
    Note over P,DB: Album ambiguity is preserved as a quality flag, not silently guessed.
    Note over T,DB: Discovery/feed omission never means deletion.<br/>Auth/rate/transport/5xx leave pending missing unchanged.
